{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1117202-jazz-age-changeling-the-dreaming-my-notes","id":1117202,"title":"Jazz Age Changeling The Dreaming (My Notes)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-17T08:16:49-07:00","id":1117202,"title":"Jazz Age Changeling The Dreaming (My Notes)","content":"This is a setting I have been pondering. It is pre-Resurgence, and so the Dreaming is primarily hinged on the Big Themes of the Roaring Twenties. Big goings-on were underway, social and economic upheaval, unions, gangsters, speakeasies, entertainment and all manner of craziness was everywhere.<br /> <br /> <b>THE SETTING IN GENERAL</b><br /> It is the 1920's, The Roaring Twenties. An age of social, artistic and cultural dynamism. It was a time that saw unprecedented industrial and economic growth, celebrity and music. It was a world of Art Deco design, automobiles, flappers, gangsters, moving pictures and jazz music. Everything and everything seemed within reach, even magic. In this era between the Great Wars and before the Resurgence, the Dreaming is hot with turmoil. The America of this era is either the industrial Dream of the cities, full of huge sky-scrapers and machine chimera, or the vast Dreaming of Purple Mountains, Hobo Jungles and Fruited Plains. Most trods through this landscape are wild places and trecherous, with the safest being sky trods or those still owned by the Nunnehi.<br /> The Changelings of this era would be deeply involved in the many creative elements of the time. The post war era was full of creative energy, tragedy, literature, conflict and a growing romanticism. Speakeasies, Nickelodeon Theaters, Burlesque and Vaudeville would all be tremendous sources of glamour, and the dreams of Industry and the hopes of Immigrants as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>NEW YORK, THE DREAMING CITY </b><br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/57/d1/cf/57d1cf5ba63a009a5936356fcd103c41--urbanism-comics.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> New York (including Manhattan, Brooklyn, Queens, the Bronx and Staten Island) city of the 20's was a place of HUGE ideas, and this is reflected in the Near Dreaming. Skyscrapers even bigger than their real counterparts make the city feel like a colossal canyon, with airships and dragons bustling for space in the skyline. Mechanical chimera, like combinations of trolleys and beetles scurry along routes and mechanical spiders stalk the buildings. The air is crackling with energy, both good and very dangerous. The fae of New York City are politically centered around Goblin Town, with this Nocker freehold being very powerful in both fae and mortal society. Most powerful fae in America will be Unseelie, playing the part of dream thieves and fairy kidnappers in the form of sweatshops, slumlords and the cruel entertainment industries to crush the dreams out of mortals, all to feed the ravenous dreams of the Jazz Age.<br /> Several societies are active in the Dreaming City of New York, that have some connection with Mortal and Prodigal groups, such as:<br /> <i><b>The Knights of St. Tammany (Secret Society)- </b></i>This society is politically linked to Tammany Hall, a political organization dedicated to the welfare of Irish immigrants and citizens. The Knights of St Tammany are dedicated to the fostering of the Dreams of Ireland and America. They are close allies with the <a href=\"http://bandaiyan.wikia.com/wiki/Tuatha_de_Fionn\" target=\"_blank\">Tuatha de Fionn</a> (Fianna) and the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Sept_of_the_Green\" target=\"_blank\">Sept of the Green</a> (Bone Gnawers), and also have contacts among the mages of <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/House_Ex_Miscellanea\" target=\"_blank\">House Ex Miscellanea</a>. The Knights of St. Tammany is composed of Clurichaun, Piskie, Pooka, Redcap, Selkie and Troll members. Kinain members are numerous, as are some Fianna kinfolk.<br /> <i><b>The White Tree Fellowship (Secret Society)- </b></i>A society that made pacts with the Nunnehi of the Northeast states that holds true to this day (though often strained). Members of the White Tree Fellowship endeavor to bridge gaps between the Kithain and the Nunnehi, particularly the May-may-gwya-shi and Rock Giants (many of whom live in Manhattan as builders).<br /> <br /> <b>OTHER CITIES</b><br /> Most of this setting will revolve around New York and Chicago with occasional forays to New Orleans, San Francisco and Los Angeles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Kithain </b><br /> Classical myth and folktales are part of the normal curriculum of this era. This along with the influx of Old World refugees coming to the Americas brings with it a potent openness to the fae. Most people don\u2019t believe in fairies, but the dreams associated with them is not so distant.<br /> <b>Autumn Sidhe-</b> The Sidhe of this era would come from House Scathach and House Liam, having stayed behind on Earth. A distinctly American House, The American Dream is also a possibility.<br /> <b>Boggans-</b> Right away the \u201cGoodfellas and Goombahs\u201d sidebar in Kithbook Boggan comes immediately to mind for this setting.<br /> <b>Clurichaun</b><b>-</b> The Irish were deeply involved in the more energetic movements of the 20\u2019s. Gangsters, entertainers, immigrants and Unions. The Clurichaun are quite numerous.<br /> <b>Eshu-</b> One Thousand and One Nights (or Arabian Knights) is very popular in the Jazz Age, and along with tales of Gypsy wanderers and dark-eyed lovers, the Eshu are doing quite well.<br /> <b>Nockers-</b> These fae are very active and very wealthy in this era, riding on the creativity of invention and industry. The Unseelie Freehold of Goblin Town is mighty in Kithain affairs.<br /> <b>Piskies-</b> Along with the Clurichaun and Selkies, the Piskies come with their Irish kin. With pixies presence in J.M. Berry\u2019s Peter Pan, Piskies have gained a certain glamour boost.<br /> <b>Pooka-</b> This fae are widespread in the Jazz Age, often finding work in Nickelodeon Theaters, travelling shows and the newspaper reporters are common occupations. Away from the cities, Songs of the South have invigorated this kith.<br /> <b>Redcap-</b> The horrors of WWI and the terror haunted dreams of its survivors have invigorated these fae. Gangsters, Union leg breakers, and Moon-shiners (brewing the \u201cgoing-blind\u201d kind of booze) are common occupations for Redcaps.<br /> <b>Satyrs-</b> Greek myth is widely taught in this era, and Satyrs are often depicted is newspaper cartoons. Most Satyrs work as entertainers, especially Burlesque theaters.<br /> <b>Selkies-</b> Along with the Clurichaun and Piskies, these fae come with their Irish kin.<br /> <b>Sluagh-</b> The Sluagh are widespread in the Jazz Age, dwelling among immigrants. Tales of people living underground, or dwelling among dead things is ever-present specters.<br /> <b>Trolls-</b> Trolls are often leaders in Kithain society, holding elected positions and even noble titles.<br /> <br /> Others<br /> <b>Korred-</b> These Celtic fae are rare, but are not unheard of. They dwell mostly in libraries, and are often involved in education and the establishment of schools and libraries.<br /> <b>Morganed-</b> These sea fae are seaside folk, and so make great sailors. Many live on the island of Manhattan and in Boston, close to the sea that they need.<br /> <b>River Hag-</b> These nasty fae love water and dank places where they can have access to prey and the water. Manhattan and New Jersey has a number of these fae, who love its many docks and underground places.<br /> <b>Witchel-</b> Though a minority, these old world fae are present, and have most of their number among Norse immigrants. Many of this kith have found work in the Coal mines of the Southeast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-18-2017, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T09:05:16-07:00","id":1117229,"title":"","content":"<b>The American Dream (House)</b><br /> <img src=\"https://carlanthonyonlinedotcom.files.wordpress.com/2013/06/miss-columbia-turns-to-uncle-sam-with-her-problem.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> The American Dream is intrinsically tied to the BIG DREAMS of the Nation. And after WWI those dreams are hot and powerful. Unlike other houses, this house is dedicated to a powerful spirit, that of America itself, also known as America the Beautiful. This spirit is seen by the fae as a powerful Chimera, but to the Nunnehi and the Fera, it is an Incarna spirit of growing strength. When manifested, this spirit appears as an Uncle Sam like figure. An old but vigorous man with a white beard. He is stern but prone to smiling, and usually accompanied by ferocious Eagle chimera. Members of this House are very active in the Jazz Age, seeking to be motivators of the Big Dreams of America, promoting forward action as much as possible.<br /> Autumn Sidhe and Commoner Fae are all members of this house, with no distinction between them in the eyes of the houses spiritual patron. All must embody the desires of the American Dream to grow in power and influence. In the years leading up to the Resurgence, the American Dream will begin taking Fera as children, becoming a powerful Totem. After the Resurgence this spirit is no longer directly active in Fae affairs.<br /> <b>Boon:</b> Members of this House can never become lost, and even abroad Americans make an extra effort to help him. The ST may have Ma and Pa America show up just as the character is about to be thrown into jail, pay his bail, and give him money to buy a bus ticket back home. Difficulties involving interactions with public officials, government officials, or police - anyone who has sworn an oath to uphold and defend the Constitution of the United States of America - are decreased by three.<br /> <b>Ban:</b> The downside to this totem is that devotees must make a Stamina and Survival roll (diff 7) at each new moon to avoid becoming instantly addicted to something of the ST's choosing (beer, burlesque, cigarettes, etc). They also begin to adopt a swaggering demeanor, tell other people what to do, and often cheat at cards, taxes and cgames.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 09-13-2017, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T18:36:34-07:00","id":1117528,"title":"","content":"Once again, cool stuff! I recently ran a session in 1927 Chicago and really enjoyed the setting.<br /> <br /> However, would there really be a need for a new noble House? Especially one so specific to a country and time period?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T18:49:32-07:00","id":1117530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1117202-jazz-age-changeling-the-dreaming-my-notes?p=1117528#post1117528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, cool stuff! I recently ran a session in 1927 Chicago and really enjoyed the setting.<br /> <br /> However, would there really be a need for a new noble House? Especially one so specific to a country and time period?</div> </div> </div> </div>Struggled with that, as this is a Bone Gnawer totem. But I wanted something particularly American. And without additions there would only be House Scathach and House Liam available for nobles. Uncle Sam imagery was so well represented in that era. Much to play with. <br /> <br /> There will also be other potent spirits/chimera of the age as fickle patrons. Totems such as the Rat King, Lady Liberty and Old King Coal. Being a frien of such beings is possible, but they will not have houses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-18-2017, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T07:01:35-07:00","id":1117706,"title":"","content":"<b>OLD KING COAL</b> (King Stoke)<br /> <i><img src=\"http://s3-eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/lookandlearn-preview/XR/XR509/XR509885.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> \u201cOld King Coal what are we gonna do, when the mountains are gone and so are you?\u201d</i> - Sturgill Simpson, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_5SYZeA9cxQ\" target=\"_blank\">Old King Coal</a><br /> Old King Coal is the ruthless spirit of Coal, oil and other smoke and smog producers. He is a fierce old tyrant that is intrinsically entwined in the Industrial Dream. King Coal is a throwback to ancient bloody gods, adoring living sacrifices, particularly children. Though in the modern age these sacrifices come in the form of child laborers, whose lives are crushed away far from the sight of the sun. His chief servants are the foulest of fey, and the many smog spirits and nervosa chimera. Werewolves claim that this spirit is an aspect of the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Elemental_Wyrm\" target=\"_blank\">Elemental Wyrm</a>, Hoga, but this is unconfirmed.<br /> This spirit appears as a large, powerful man who is usually wearing a smoke stack like crown and covered all over in coal dust and soot. He appears most often in industrial yards and among the smokestacks of the city, holding court among his spirits and attending fae. He is friendly to fae who approach him, particularly Nockers and Redcaps with whom he has many agreements. In the Jazz Age this spirit is still very strong, though he has been having trouble from the spirit of electricity. King Coal is active in the Courts of the more industrial, city fae, and has standing agreements with Goblin Town, and others. However this spirit is closely allied with corrupt and dangerous entities as well, and more than a few Seelie fae have run afoul of his agents.<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Strength 8, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5, Charisma 4, Manipulation 5, Appearance 4, Perception 2, Intelligence 6, Wits 5<br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Gremayre 5, Kenning 5, Law 5, Lore (City) 4, Science (Mechanical and Chemical Engineering) 5, Streetwise 5, Subterfuge 4.<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Allies 5, Contacts 5, Rank 5, Resources 5, Treasure 4.<br /> Glamour: 10, Willpower: 8, Banality 3 (Rage 8, Gnosis 10, Willpower 8)<br /> <b>Redes: </b>Armor (4 dice), Befuddle, Corruption*, Fester, Flight, Meld*, Poof Begone, Steal Glamour, Shapeshift, Wyrd. <br /> <b>Arts:</b> Autumn 5, Contracts 5, Dragons Ire 4, Legerdemain 5, Pyretics 4, Skycraft 5, Wayfare 5, Winter 3.<br /> <b>Realms: </b>Actor 5, Fae 3, Nature 2, Prop 4, Scene 5, Time 2.<br /> <b>Health Levels: </b>OK, OK, OK, -1, -1, -1, -1, -2, -2, -2, -4, Inc.<br /> <b>Attack:</b> Sword (Str+3, diff 6).<br /> <b>Corruption*: </b>By making a Glamour challenge against the target's Willpower, the spirit implants a single evil suggestion that their target must act on before the session is through. The chimera may use this Rede on mortals if it also possesses the Enchantment or Wyrd redes. This rede costs 1 willpower to use.<br /> <b>Meld*:</b> Old King Coal can merge with smoke or coal, simply disappearing into the element in question. The rede costs two Glamour and one turn to employ. At the end of that time, the element may be disturbed by the spirit\u2019s passage, but the spirit itself cannot be seen or affected. Obviously, this Rede requires a decent amount of the element in question.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> In my campaigns, beings such as Old King Coal are <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Spirit_(cWOD)\" target=\"_blank\">Umbrood</a>, and not Chimera. He is immune to Cold Iron and mortal disbelief, tough the Mists erase most encounters with mankind. Technically, King Coal is a corrupt spirit with close ties to the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Elemental_Courts\" target=\"_blank\">Elemental Court</a>. However he also works just fine as a powerful, somewhat banal chimera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-18-2017, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T13:04:54-07:00","id":1120456,"title":"","content":"Loving this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}